/* book exam traps: Loss in dB grows with length: 0.2 dB/km is not the total loss. Add and subtract dB values; never multiply powers written in dB. | dBm is an absolute power (referred to 1 mW); dB is a ratio. 4 dB of loss takes 0 dBm to −4 dBm, not to 0.4 dBm. | The source is the E/O converter and the photodetector is the O/E converter. Do not swap them in the block diagram. | 1310 nm is the low-dispersion window and 1550 nm the low-loss window; students often swap the two reasons. | Fiber's immunity to interference comes from glass being a dielectric. It does not come from the light being 'shielded' by the cladding. */
